    "summary": "Garcia shreds on Bertha and Deal, tight high‑energy set",
    "blurb": "The show delivers Garcia’s lightning‑fast solos on Bertha and Deal, backed by a driving rhythm section. Highlights include Big Boss Man, El Paso and an inspired second‑set flow after Good Lovin'. Overall the performance is high‑energy with top‑notch soundboard capture.",
    "review": "April 15, 1971 at Allegheny State College finds the Dead in fine form, feeding off the intimate gym setting where the crowd sat right on the floor. Garcia is in full shredding mode, launching scorching leads on Bertha and Deal that cut through a crisp, superb mix. The band rides a high‑energy current from Pigpen’s Good Lovin' into a rolling first set packed with Big Boss Man, El Paso and a tight Playing In The Band. The second set keeps the momentum with China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider, then moves through soulful blues numbers like Next Time You See Me before a rousing finale of Casey Jones. Even though Sugar Magnolia stumbles a bit, the overall flow is smooth and the recording captures every nuance, making this one of the standouts from the early‑70s era.",
